  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Maintenance</h3>

  <p>Routine upkeep across the Betta lineup comes down to emptying the large, easy-clean debris basket as it fills, and keeping the solar panel surface clear so charging stays efficient. Twin SCT motors are built specifically to tolerate saltwater pools, so there's no special maintenance step needed if your pool runs a salt chlorination system rather than traditional chlorine.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">Common Questions About the Betta Lineup</h3>

  <p><strong>Will a Betta skimmer work in a saltwater pool?</strong><br>
  Yes. Every model uses twin Salt Chlorine Tolerant (SCT) motors, built specifically to hold up in saltwater pools without the corrosion issues that affect equipment designed only for traditional chlorinated water.</p>

  <p><strong>Does it need to be plugged in?</strong><br>
  The Betta SE runs on solar power only. The SE Plus, Flex, and Neo all support dual charging, solar for normal operation plus a wall adapter as a backup option.</p>

  <p><strong>What's the difference between the SE Plus and the Flex?</strong><br>
  The SE Plus adds a Shallow Safeguard Design for pools with varying depth. The Flex is the more compact, lightweight model with a soft-touch casing and dual Eco/Normal cleaning modes, and it's specifically suited to infinity-edge pools.</p>

  <p><strong>Why would I choose the Neo over the other models?</strong><br>
  The Neo is the only model with full smart app control through a gateway system, letting you monitor and control it remotely, plus Weather-Adaptive Cleaning that adjusts patrol behavior to current conditions rather than running the same routine regardless of wind or debris load.</p>

  <p><strong>Does it clean the pool floor, or just the surface?</strong><br>
  Betta skimmers are built for surface skimming, collecting floating debris before it sinks. They are not floor or wall cleaners.</p>

  <p><strong>Can I finance a Betta skimmer?</strong><br>
  Yes, financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments across the Betta lineup.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Ownership, Handled</h3>

  <p>Normal Betta orders ship by parcel (orders of 12 or more units ship via freight), with a typical lead time of 1 to 2 business days. Financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments, so the cost spreads over time instead of landing as one lump sum. And you're not buying this from a manufacturer's storefront with no one to call, Yard Automation Pros provides real, US-based expert guidance before and after your purchase, from matching the right model to your pool to helping you get the most out of it once it's running. If something isn't working the way it should, you have a real person to reach, not a support ticket queue.</p>

